From: DroidDeck
Subject: [PATCH] steamcompmgr: the Steam client's window is not an SDL fullscreen shell

set_size_hints treats any override-redirect window with exactly one
InputOutput child as an old SDL fullscreen shell: it takes the child's size as
the window's size and sets ignoreOverrideRedirect. On this device the Steam
client's CEF window matches that shape - it is override-redirect (X12B
"or=1" in xinspect), 2404x1080, with one child - so the client gets
ignoreOverrideRedirect, which keeps it out of GAMESCOPE_FOCUSABLE_APPS and
leaves "focused app: none". gamescope then never composites, and a session
logs 0 GPU frames from games with no swapchain of its own.

Two things distinguish the client from an SDL shell and both hold here only
for the latter:

  * an SDL shell sizes itself from its child because it has no size hints of
    its own. The Steam client's window is already exactly the output size and
    carries Steam's STEAM_GAME atom, so its own geometry is the truth.
  * SDL reparents its game window under the shell. The client's child is its
    own render surface.

So leave a window that Steam identifies (appID 769, or any STEAM_GAME atom)
alone: keep its geometry and do not mark it ignoreOverrideRedirect.

Verified on the Pixel 10 (Tensor G5): before, "focused app: none" for the
whole session and 0 GPU frames from games; a Steam window with STEAM_GAME=769
is now a focus candidate.

--- a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
+++ b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
@@ -5598,7 +5598,10 @@
 		// SDL creates a fullscreen override-redirect window and reparents the game
 		// window under it, centered. We get rid of the modeswitch and also want that
 		// black border gone.
-		if (w->xwayland().a.override_redirect)
+		// The Steam client's CEF window is also override-redirect with one child; it is not
+		// an SDL shell (it carries STEAM_GAME and is already the output size), and taking it
+		// for one leaves "focused app: none" so nothing is composited.
+		if (w->xwayland().a.override_redirect && !window_is_steam( w ) && !win_has_game_id( w ))
 		{
 			Window	    root_return = None, parent_return = None;
 			Window	    *children = NULL;
